    "description": "ParcelHub consumes shipping events from several regional queues. Events may be JSON or Avro, and each carries a schema version, parcel identifier, weight, destination code, and optional declared value. Today QueueConsumer passes each message to RouteParcelHandler, CalculateChargeHandler, or ExceptionHandler before any validation, causing those handlers to repeat range checks and handle malformed payloads differently. A small number of events with negative weight, oversized strings, unknown versions, or invalid destination codes have reached downstream domain code. The platform team needs a single ingress component that checks payload shape, encoding, size, and permitted ranges for every message before dispatching to any handler, using versioned schemas supplied by SchemaRegistry. Validation failures must produce a dead-letter event with a reason code and must not invoke business components. The decision is whether to place these checks in the queue-consumer ingress path or in a shared handler hierarchy, given that every inbound message must pass through the checks exactly once before domain processing.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose where every inbound queue message receives schema, size, encoding, and range validation so malformed events cannot reach any business handler.",
    "notes": "Every queue message is schema- and range-validated at ingress before any handler runs (intercepting-validator); secure-base-action is the near-miss alternative the description explicitly weighs."
  },
